<article class="env-lemma" id="0EZ9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EZ9">Lemma <span data-tag="0EZ9">21.30.2</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0EZ3" data-tag="0EZ3">21.30.1</a> for $X$ in $\mathcal{C}$ denote $\mathcal{A}_ X$ the objects of $\textit{Ab}(\mathcal{C}_\tau /X)$ of the form $\epsilon _ X^{-1}\mathcal{F}'$ with $\mathcal{F}'$ in $\mathcal{A}'_ X$. Then </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
for $\mathcal{F}$ in $\textit{Ab}(\mathcal{C}_\tau /X)$ we have $\mathcal{F} \in \mathcal{A}_ X \Leftrightarrow \epsilon _{X, *}\mathcal{F} \in \mathcal{A}'_ X$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$f_\tau ^{-1}$ sends $\mathcal{A}_ Y$ into $\mathcal{A}_ X$ for any morphism $f : X \to Y$ of $\mathcal{C}$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Part (1) follows from (<a href="/tag/0EZ6" data-tag="0EZ6">3</a>) and part (2) follows from (<a href="/tag/0EZ5" data-tag="0EZ5">2</a>) and the commutativity of (<a href="/tag/0EZ2" data-tag="0EZ2">21.30.0.1</a>) which gives $\epsilon _ X^{-1} \circ f_{\tau '}^{-1} = f_\tau ^{-1} \circ \epsilon _ Y^{-1}$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>